{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-mixed-demo-review", "file": "references/seed-motif-generator-checkpoint.md", "content": "# Seed-motif generator checkpoint after a wrong submission

A salient colored seed embedded in a noisy grid does not by itself imply a copy rule. Candidate classes can include translated shape occurrences, periodic/lattice replication, directional rays, or combinations. Before extrapolating, record the seed's exact coordinates and the complete input/output difference mask in every demo. Verify both positive and negative cases: why each changed cell is selected, and why visually similar unchanged cells are excluded. Check palettes and dimensions that vary across demos; distinguish the seed color, target/background color, and unrelated noise empirically rather than assuming one role from a single pair.

After an incorrect submission, discard the whole generator. Do not move a few cells, swap a presumed background color, or switch to a nearby geometric interpretation without replaying it against every demo. With a costly attempt budget, use remaining demos for explicit competing hypotheses and only submit after a full-mask validation. Preserve all cells outside the supported transformation and verify dimensions/row lengths.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-seq0/frozen/seen/play/users/u010/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-mixed-demo-review/references/seed-motif-generator-checkpoint.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-evidence-workflow", "file": "references/session-lesson.md", "content": "# Session lesson: motif resemblance is not a generator

In a Continual-ARC stream, a series of heterogeneous examples can tempt the solver to label each task as colored-template copying based on a few salient placements. One predicted mask can even look plausible on the test while failing because its translation/target assumptions were not checked against the complete examples. The reliable method is to extract the exact seed and complete diff for each pair, separate target eligibility from shape and placement, and enumerate candidates against all changed and unchanged cells. Integrate each new pair immediately; do not spend most of the demo budget on reflexive requests. After wrong feedback, discard the whole rule and make a materially revised inference rather than repeating nearby guesses. Keep every puzzle turn to exactly one action JSON object.

